  "assessment": "The only observed source view is the street-front elevation; side, rear, roof surface and interior are inferred and are not treated as source facts. Current front keeps the seven upper rows, three-pier/two-bay count, garage/entry positions and open roof terrace, but it changes the left-bay balconies into shallow white-framed units, shortens the roof screen, and renders the right-bay glazing as uniform opaque dark green without the visible beige curtain/inner layer. The current ground-floor blank band and door heights are hard to verify from the low-resolution front view, so they are not ranked above these clear mismatches. No source evidence supports adding a canopy, lower annex or pitched roof.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "priority": 1,
      "view": "front",
      "problem": "The left bay reads as stacked shallow white-framed window/balcony boxes, not the source's 4650-wide, 1500-deep full-width balcony recesses with transparent glass balustrades and shadowed interiors.",
      "action": "Deepen each left-bay opening to 1500, remove window-like white framing/mullions, keep one wide opening per floor, add a 1100 frameless glass rail with a thin top rail at the front edge, dark recessed interior and planters inside; retain the seven rows and slab bands."
    },
    {
      "priority": 2,
      "view": "oblique",
      "problem": "The rooftop screen is a shallow black railing, whereas the source's silhouette is defined by a 700 concrete parapet plus a 2200-high fine vertical metal screen around the terrace.",
      "action": "Raise the perimeter grille to 2200 above the parapet with thin vertical bars and top/bottom rails, keep the roof open with planters, and do not add a solid roof or canopy."
    },
    {
      "priority": 3,
      "view": "front",
      "problem": "The right-bay glazing is uniformly opaque dark green; the source shows reflective/transparent floor-to-ceiling glass with beige curtains and a lighter inner layer visible behind it.",
      "action": "Set the glass to 2400 high with a 100 sill and thin dark frames/200 mullion, add semi-transparent beige curtain planes behind the glass, and retain two windows per floor."
    }
  ],
  "keep": [
    "The seven upper residential rows and three-pier/two-bay front composition are present and correctly ordered.",
    "The right-bay garage shutter and left-bay recessed entry occupy the correct first-floor positions.",
    "The open roof terrace and planter boxes are present and should not be replaced by a solid roof or canopy.",
    "The inferred side and rear window grids are internally coherent with the front structural grid."
  ],
